<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Super Group lifts half yr shr, no div.</title>
<headline>Super Group lifts half yr shr, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     14.2	  vs    12.4</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   20.11	 vs     3.54</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   25.94	 vs     5.44</p>
<p>    Tax			  5.83	 vs     1.90</p>
<p>    Turnover		 651.46	 vs   153.76</p>
<p>    Full name:   Super Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The policy of the group is not to pay an interim dividend. Dividends paid in respect of the full year will be at least three times covered.</p>
<p>Further to the cautionary announcements in September and October shareholders are advised that negotiations are in progressing. If successful, these negotiations could lead to the acquisition of a company with a dollar denomination revenue flow. Accordingly, shareholders are advised to continue exercising caution when dealing in their Super Group shares.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
